  "tSlideFormHelpTheoryTitle": "The title appears at the very top of the student screen.\n- Keep it concise and specific, max 120 characters.\n- Name the core concept, not the chapter name.",
  "tSlideFormHelpTheoryContent": "How to write lesson content:\n- Separate paragraphs with one blank line.\n- Lines starting with \"- \" or \"* \" automatically become list items.\n- Otherwise text is shown as-is: **bold**, # headings, links, and `code` are not formatted.\n\nExample:\nHTML is a markup language for building web pages.\n\n- Tags are opened then closed.\n- Attributes attach to the opening tag.",
  "tSlideFormHelpCodeFileSample": "Only determines the file name on the code card:\n- HTML → index.html\n- CSS → style.css\n- JavaScript → script.js\n- Python → script.py",
  "tSlideFormHelpSampleCode": "Sample code shown in the code box below the explanation.\n- Leave empty if the slide needs no code sample.\n- Write the raw code only, without markdown block markers.\n- Max 8000 characters.",
  "tSlideFormHelpExerciseTitle": "The title appears in the exercise header, max 120 characters.\nExample: \"Complete the HTML Closing Tag\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpShortInstruction": "One or two sentences of guidance before the student taps a slot.\n- Explain which part must be completed.\n- Do not mention the answer here.",
  "tSlideFormHelpCodeTemplate": "Paste code here, then mark blanks with ___1___, ___2___, and so on.\n- Markers are recognized as long as they use at least two underscores at the start and end, with an optional number in the middle.\n- Slot order follows their order of appearance in the code.\n- One slot means one answer; do not place two slots for the same answer.\n\nExample:\nx = ___1___\nprint(x)",
  "tSlideFormHelpSlotAnswers": "Fill in the correct answer for each slot in order of appearance.\n- Leading/trailing spaces are ignored, but letter case matters: write \"print\", not \"Print\".\n- Write exactly what should appear in the code.\n- The number of entries follows the number of detected slots.",
  "tSlideFormHelpDistractors": "Extra words that appear as choices, but are not the correct answer.\n- Separate with commas.\n- Distractors identical to the key are discarded automatically.\n- Keep at least one so students really have to choose.",
  "tSlideFormHelpCodeFile": "Determines the file name on the code card:\n- HTML → index.html\n- CSS → style.css\n- JavaScript → script.js\n- Python → script.py",
  "tSlideFormHelpQuestionTitle": "The title appears in the exercise header, max 120 characters.\nExample: \"Python Variable Declaration\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpInteractiveInstruction": "Brief guidance students read before typing.\n- Say what to look for without giving the answer.\n- Max 300 characters.",
  "tSlideFormHelpQuestionCode": "Write a code snippet, then replace the part to fill in with [KETIK_DISINI].\n- That marker becomes an input box on the student screen.\n- More than one marker per slide is allowed.\n- Without a marker, students have nowhere to type an answer.",
  "tSlideFormHelpAnswerKeyword": "The answer considered correct.\n- Comparison ignores leading/trailing spaces and letter case, so \"Print\" equals \"print\".\n- Enter a single keyword or short expression only.",
  "tSlideFormHelpWrongHint": "Help shown when a student answer is wrong.\n- Give directional hints, do not write the answer directly.\n- One or two sentences are enough.",
  "tSlideFormHelpSlideTitle": "The title appears in the slide header, max 120 characters.\nExample: \"Guess the Modulo Operator Output\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpChallengeInstruction": "A short question above the code block.\nUsually enough: \"What output is printed to the terminal?\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpSourceCode": "Code students read to guess the output.\n- Write it exactly like the original program.\n- Code is only displayed, not run, so the result must be guessable from the code content.",
  "tSlideFormHelpOutputChoices": "Fill in all four choices (A to D).\n- Tap the circle on the left to mark the answer key.\n- One choice must exactly match the actual output.\n- Do not leave choices empty: empty choices still appear on the student screen.",
  "tSlideFormHelpOutputExplanation": "Appears after students answer, right or wrong.\nExplain why that output appears, e.g. operation order or the data types involved.",
  "tSlideFormHelpChallengeTitle": "The title appears in the challenge header, max 120 characters.\nExample: \"Finding the For Loop Bug\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpScenario": "Brief context of the problem students face; shown as instructions above the code.\nDescribe the situation, do not mention the wrong line number.",
  "tSlideFormHelpBuggyCode": "The full code containing the bug.\n- Line numbers count from 1 following the line order in this box, including blank lines.\n- Insert a bug that can genuinely be explained by \"Error Type\" and \"Fix Code\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpTargetLine": "The correct line number, counted from 1.\n- Must be between 1 and the number of code lines above.\n- If out of range, the student screen locks to the nearest line so answers never match.",
  "tSlideFormHelpErrorType": "Error category label shown to students.\nExample: SyntaxError, IndentationError, NameError.",
  "tSlideFormHelpBugHint": "This text becomes the explanation shown after students answer.\n- Explain the rule violated on that line.\n- If left empty, \"Valid Fix Code\" is used as the explanation.",
  "tSlideFormHelpFixCode": "The correct fix snippet for the marked line.\n- Used as a solution example and backup explanation when \"Indicator Message\" is empty.\n- Write only the fixed part, not the whole program.",
  "tSlideFormHelpQuizTitle": "The title appears in the quiz header, max 120 characters.\nExample: \"Understanding Data Types\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpQuizQuestion": "A question with one correct answer.\n- Ask about a single concept only, do not combine.\n- Max 300 characters.",
  "tSlideFormHelpAnswerChoices": "Fill in all four choices (A to D).\n- Tap the circle on the left to mark the answer key.\n- Do not leave choices empty, as they still appear as empty options on the student screen.",
  "tSlideFormHelpFeedback": "Appears after students answer, right or wrong.\nExplain why the answer key is correct and, if needed, why the distractors are wrong.",
  "tSlideFormHelpOutroTitle": "The title appears in the closing slide header, max 120 characters.\nExample: \"Chapter Summary\".",
  "tSlideFormHelpSummary": "A summary students read at the end of the chapter.\n- Revisit the main concepts just learned.\n- Give a motivating close, not a new question.",
  "tSlideFormHelpMasteredConcepts": "List of concepts considered mastered after this chapter.\n- Separate with commas, e.g.: Variables, Loops.\n- Each concept appears as an achievement label.\n- Enter at least one concept.",
